   Everything in this template is STATIC across a run so it can be prompt-cached:
   the clause itself travels in the user message, not here. With ~1,500 clauses per
   circular that turns one cache write into ~1,499 cheap reads.

   Note what is *not* asked for: the citation. Page, char_span and clause_path are
   attached by the pipeline from the clause that was sent, so the model cannot
   invent a source. It is asked only for what it can read off the text in front of
   it, plus the verbatim sentence it took each field from.
